  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q32-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "32",
    "prompt": "The length of a room is 8 m greater than its width.\nIf both the length and the width are increased by 2 m, the area increases by $60\\text{ m}^2$.\nFind the dimensions of the room.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Width $10\\text{ m}$; length $18\\text{ m}$. Expanding the area equation gives $L+W=28$, with $L=W+8$.",
      "worked": "Let $W$ and $L$ be the width and length in metres.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nL&=W+8\\\\\n(L+2)(W+2)&=LW+60\\\\\nLW+2L+2W+4&=LW+60\\\\\n2L+2W&=56\\\\\nL+W&=28\\\\\n(W+8)+W&=28\\\\\n2W&=20\\\\\nW&=10\\\\\nL&=10+8=18\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe width is $10\\text{ m}$ and the length is $18\\text{ m}$.\nCheck: $20\\times12-18\\times10=60\\text{ m}^2$, and both dimensions are positive.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
